<title>FRANCE: French May consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>French May consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following final data:</p>
<p>				    May	  Apr	May 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.2	  0.0	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     0.9	  0.9	  2.4</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    115.2	115.0	114.2</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    108.2   0.8    0.6    0.6</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    108.9  -0.1    0.4   -0.1</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    124.6   0.3    0.6    1.7</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    111.8  -0.4   -2.0    1.4</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    127.2   0.0    0.8    3.0</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    128.5   0.1    0.2    1.6</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    109.7   0.1    0.3    0.5</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.3   0.2    0.3    0.7</p>
<p>				    May   Last 3 months  yr/yr</p>
<p> EU harmonised		  0.1	  0.2	  0.9</p>
<p>				    May	 April	 May 96</p>
<p> EU harmonised infl. indx 101.2	101.1	100.3</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
